From core k278: core engines now honor user_agent_timeout on Net::Async::HTTP, but knarr's own _http client (raw passthrough, Langfuse tracing, ACP/A2A calls) has no timeout — a hanging upstream stalls the client connection forever. Add a configurable upstream timeout (config + env), total for non-streaming, stall_timeout for streaming passthrough (Net::Async::HTTP per-request options), tracing with a short timeout so telemetry can't stall requests. Tests with a never-answering local server.
